          },
          "summary": "Updates by themselves. When a newer Anvira is published, a small button appears at the top right. Click it to download, then again to restart into the new version. Nothing downloads or restarts until you click.…",
          "highlights": [
            {
              "kind": "New",
              "text": "Updates by themselves"
            },
            {
              "kind": "New",
              "text": "Runtime updates"
            },
            {
              "kind": "New",
              "text": "Optional account"
            }
          ],
          "notes": [
            {
              "title": "New",
              "html": "<ul><li><strong>Updates by themselves.</strong> When a newer Anvira is published, a small button appears at the top right. Click it to download, then again to restart into the new version. Nothing downloads or restarts until you click. <strong>Settings → About → Check for updates</strong> looks right now.</li><li><strong>Runtime updates.</strong> A second button appears when a newer Anvira Runtime is available. It updates the AI engine in place; your models and settings are kept.</li><li><strong>Optional account.</strong> Sign in or create an account from the sidebar or <strong>Settings → Account</strong>. Everything still works without one, and your chats and files stay on your PC.</li></ul>"
            },
            {
              "title": "Fixed",
              "html": "<ul><li>The window now always fits your screen and remembers where you left it (it could hang off the right or bottom edge).</li><li>The composer &quot;+&quot; menu and dialogs are no longer cut off on small screens.</li><li>The Search page quick-jump buttons work again.</li><li>The start-up animation is smoother and the first-run dialog waits for it.</li><li>Memory recall across chats works.</li><li>A dropped connection to the AI engine now says what happened (&quot;The AI engine stopped in the middle of the answer&quot;) with a hint, instead of a bare &quot;terminated&quot;.</li><li>Very long messages fold up behind <strong>Show more</strong> so one big paste does not take over the screen.</li></ul>"
            }
          ]
        },
